Data for "enchantment install init systemd" (enchant_install_init in
lib/lib.install). Everything here is written into the target before sorcery
casts anything there:

  depends   answers for sorcery, one "spell:dependency:on|off" per line.
            A recorded answer in the target's depends database is changed
            in place (it would win otherwise); anything else goes into
            /var/state/sorcery/default_depends.
  presets/  spell option files, appended to /etc/sorcery/local/depends/
            (only VAR="value" lines: sorcery rewrites these files word by
            word, so comments turn into garbage). linux-pam's
            PAM_CHKPWD_SUID=y makes unix_chkpwd setuid root, so programs
            running as the user (screen lockers) can check passwords
  pam.d/    the PAM stack: a shared system-auth (and system-login for login
            services, which adds pam_systemd), copied to /etc/pam.d/
            (sorcery installs a spell's own pam.d files only when missing,
            so these stay)
  sysctl.d/ copied to /etc/sysctl.d/: kernel.printk 4 4 1 7, so the kernel's
            audit notices for systemd's BPF programs stay off the console
  recast    spells recompiled (cast -c) if installed, so they pick up
            systemd (units, libsystemd) and PAM
